<X3D ...> <Scene> ... </Scene> </X3D>.

We'll include a Viewpoint.

We'll create the lawn.

Then define the wall and crenel shapes at the top of the scene? In X3D, you can define DEF nodes anywhere in the scene graph, but they must be defined before USE. Typically you put them in the scene as children of a Group or directly under Scene, but they are not rendered unless used? Actually a DEF node is still rendered if it's in the scene graph. To avoid rendering the prototype, we can put them inside a Group that is not rendered? But there's no "library" node in X3D 4.0. Usually you define them in the scene and they appear at their location. To avoid that, you can put them inside a Switch with whichChoice=-1, or just place them at a far away location. But simpler: we can define them as part of the first wall and then USE them elsewhere. But the first wall will have the wall shape as a child, and we can DEF it there. Then for other walls, we USE that shape. However, a Shape node can only have one parent. If we DEF a Shape in one Transform, we cannot USE it in another Transform because a node can only have one parent. In X3D, USE creates a new instance? Actually USE creates a reference to the same node, but a node can only have one parent. So you cannot USE a node in multiple places if it's already a child of another node. The typical pattern is to DEF a prototype (like a Group or Transform) and then USE it. But you can DEF a Shape and then USE it multiple times only if the Shape is not directly in the scene graph? Wait, in X3D, a node can be referenced by multiple parents if it's a "shared" node? The spec says: "A node that is referenced by a USE statement shall not be a child of any other node." So you must DEF a node that is not a child of another node (i.e., it's a top-level node in the scene, or inside a Group that is not rendered? Actually you can DEF a node at the top level of the Scene (direct child of Scene) and then USE it multiple times. But then that node will be rendered at its original location as well. To avoid that, you can put the DEF inside a Group that is not traversed? There's no standard way. Common practice: define the shared nodes inside a Group at the top of the Scene, and then USE them. The Group will be traversed, so the DEF nodes will be rendered once at their location (which is at origin). To avoid that, you can put them inside a Switch with whichChoice = -1. But that adds complexity.

Alternatively, we can DEF the geometry (Box) and Appearance (Material) separately, and then create new Shape nodes that USE the geometry and appearance. That's allowed: you can DEF a Box geometry and USE it in multiple Shape nodes. Similarly for Material. That is better: DEF the Box geometry for wall (size 20 5 1) and DEF a Material for wall. Then each wall Shape can USE the geometry and material. Similarly for crenel: DEF a Box geometry (1 1 1) and USE the same material.

That satisfies "built from boxes with DEF and USE". We'll DEF the Box nodes and Material nodes.

Let's do:

<Box DEF='WallBox' size='20 5 1'/>
<Material DEF='WallMaterial' diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/>
<Box DEF='CrenelBox' size='1 1 1'/>
<!-- Use same material for crenels -->

Then for each wall, we create a Shape with USE of WallBox and WallMaterial. For crenels, Shape with USE of CrenelBox and WallMaterial.

But we also need to position them. We'll use Transform nodes.

We'll also need to define the tower geometries: Cylinder and Cone. We can just write them directly.

Gatehouse: Box for body, Box for doorway.

Flag: Cylinder for pole, Box for flag.

Now, let's write the full X3D.

We'll keep node count low.

We'll structure:

<Scene>
<Viewpoint .../>
<!-- Lawn -->
<Transform translation='0 -0.05 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.2 0.6 0.2'/></Appearance>
<Box size='100 0.1 100'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>

<!-- Definitions for shared geometry and material -->
<Box DEF='WallBox' size='20 5 1'/>
<Material DEF='WallMaterial' diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/>
<Box DEF='CrenelBox' size='1 1 1'/>
<Material DEF='CrenelMaterial' diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/> <!-- could reuse WallMaterial but separate DEF for clarity -->

<!-- Tower 1: back-left -->
<Transform translation='-10 0 10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/></Appearance>
<Cylinder radius='2' height='10'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='0 10 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.4 0.2 0.2'/></Appearance>
<Cone bottomRadius='2' height='5'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Tower 2: back-right -->
<Transform translation='10 0 10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/></Appearance>
<Cylinder radius='2' height='10'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='0 10 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.4 0.2 0.2'/></Appearance>
<Cone bottomRadius='2' height='5'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Tower 3: front-right (tallest) -->
<Transform translation='10 0 -10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/></Appearance>
<Cylinder radius='2' height='15'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='0 15 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.4 0.2 0.2'/></Appearance>
<Cone bottomRadius='2' height='5'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<!-- Flag pole and flag -->
<Transform translation='0 20 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.3 0.3 0.3'/></Appearance>
<Cylinder radius='0.1' height='5'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='0 5 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='1 0 0'/></Appearance>
<Box size='2 1 0.1'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Tower 4: front-left -->
<Transform translation='-10 0 -10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/></Appearance>
<Cylinder radius='2' height='10'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='0 10 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.4 0.2 0.2'/></Appearance>
<Cone bottomRadius='2' height='5'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Walls -->
<!-- Front wall (z=-10) -->
<Transform translation='0 2.5 -10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='WallMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='WallBox'/>
</Shape>
<!-- Crenels -->
<Transform translation='-8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='-4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='0 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Back wall (z=10) -->
<Transform translation='0 2.5 10'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='WallMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='WallBox'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='-8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='-4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='0 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Left wall (x=-10) rotated 90 deg -->
<Transform translation='-10 2.5 0' rotation='0 1 0 1.5708'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='WallMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='WallBox'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='-8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='-4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='0 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Right wall (x=10) rotated 90 deg -->
<Transform translation='10 2.5 0' rotation='0 1 0 1.5708'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='WallMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='WallBox'/>
</Shape>
<Transform translation='-8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='-4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='0 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='4 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
<Transform translation='8 3 0'>
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material USE='CrenelMaterial'/></Appearance>
<Box USE='CrenelBox'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

<!-- Gatehouse on front wall (centered at x=0, z=-10) -->
<Transform translation='0 4 -10'>
<!-- Gatehouse body -->
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0.6 0.6 0.6'/></Appearance>
<Box size='6 8 3'/>
</Shape>
<!-- Dark doorway on front face -->
<Transform translation='0 0 -1.55'> <!-- front face of gatehouse at z = -1.5 (half depth 1.5) plus 0.05 offset -->
<Shape>
<Appearance><Material diffuseColor='0 0 0'/></Appearance>
<Box size='2 4 0.1'/>
</Shape>
</Transform>
</Transform>

</Scene>
</X3D>